WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.360 --> 00:00:07.420
In 2024, humanity spent two point seven two trillion dollars on war.

2
00:00:08.240 --> 00:00:15.780
That is not a typo. It is the budget for your species' favorite expensive hobby: organized violence.

3
00:00:16.900 --> 00:00:23.620
If you stacked that money in one-dollar bills, you could build a bridge two-thirds of the way to the Moon.

4
00:00:24.860 --> 00:00:35.340
You spend enough on weapons to pave a road to space. Yet you can’t figure out how to stop dying from diseases we know how

5
00:00:35.340 --> 00:00:43.220
to cure. And that’s just the money you spend on purpose. The Pentagon has lost two point five trillion dollars.

6
00:00:44.060 --> 00:00:52.620
Not spent. Lost. Like car keys, except these car keys could cure cancer hundreds of times over.

7
00:00:53.780 --> 00:00:58.220
This chapter is the receipt. A credit card bill for self-destruction.

8
00:00:59.180 --> 00:01:03.040
Instead of coffee and books, you bought missiles and robots.

9
00:01:03.800 --> 00:01:11.370
Instead of interest, you pay in human lives. And unlike a credit card, you can't declare bankruptcy.

10
00:01:11.620 --> 00:01:21.420
You just keep paying. The Itemized Receipt for Armageddon. The costs of war look like a grocery receipt from a shop that

11
00:01:21.420 --> 00:01:27.120
only sells things that explode. Everything has a price. None of it is food.

12
00:01:28.100 --> 00:01:37.980
The Shopping List (2024 Global Data). Military Personnel Salaries were six hundred eighty-one point five billion dollars.

13
00:01:38.700 --> 00:01:42.600
The cost per capita was eighty-seven dollars and thirty-seven cents.

14
00:01:43.280 --> 00:01:51.120
The daily cost was one point eight seven billion dollars. This is based on global armed forces of twenty-eight point four

15
00:01:51.120 --> 00:01:57.240
million multiplied by an average salary of twenty-four thousand dollars, adjusted for inflation.

16
00:01:59.000 --> 00:02:03.160
Weapons Procurement was six hundred fifty-four point three billion dollars.

17
00:02:04.120 --> 00:02:07.140
The cost per capita was eighty-three dollars and eighty-eight cents.

18
00:02:08.120 --> 00:02:15.780
The daily cost was one point seven nine billion dollars. This is based on the Stockholm International Peace Research Institute,

19
00:02:15.860 --> 00:02:24.900
or S.I.P.R.I. Arms Transfer Database aggregation. Operations and Maintenance was five hundred seventy-nine point eight billion

20
00:02:24.900 --> 00:02:29.180
dollars. The cost per capita was seventy-four dollars and thirty-three cents.

21
00:02:30.020 --> 00:02:38.040
The daily cost was one point five nine billion dollars. This is based on NATO standardized operations and maintenance ratios

22
00:02:38.040 --> 00:02:46.200
multiplied by global spending. Military Infrastructure was five hundred twenty point four billion dollars.

23
00:02:46.920 --> 00:02:50.480
The cost per capita was sixty-six dollars and seventy-two cents.

24
00:02:51.220 --> 00:02:58.760
The daily cost was one point four three billion dollars. This is based on base construction and maintenance across four

25
00:02:58.760 --> 00:03:08.140
thousand four hundred thirty-five major facilities. Intelligence Operations was two hundred eighty-two billion dollars.

26
00:03:08.600 --> 00:03:12.160
The cost per capita was thirty-six dollars and fifteen cents.

27
00:03:12.960 --> 00:03:21.540
The daily cost was zero point seven seven billion dollars. This is based on an estimated ten point four percent of total

28
00:03:21.540 --> 00:03:30.580
military budgets. Total Direct Military Spending: two thousand seven hundred eighteen billion dollars.

29
00:03:31.960 --> 00:03:41.710
The Equation of Immediate Destruction. The basic math for direct war costs looks like this: Here is what those letters mean,

30
00:03:41.880 --> 00:03:48.620
in case you find algebra comforting: Military Spending: The money for soldiers, bombs, and fast jets.

31
00:03:49.960 --> 00:03:56.120
Infrastructure Damage: The cost to rebuild the cities, bridges, and power plants you just blew up.

32
00:03:56.840 --> 00:04:02.960
You build them, blow them up, build them again. It is the world's most expensive form of recycling.

33
00:04:04.440 --> 00:04:14.500
Human Casualties: The value of lost lives. Even economists, who disagree about everything, agree that dead people are bad

34
00:04:14.500 --> 00:04:20.839
for business. Trade Disruption: The money lost when bombs interrupt commerce.

35
00:04:21.380 --> 00:04:26.980
Trucks cannot truck when the road is a crater. Current Annual Calculation.

36
