T disruption equals six hundred sixteen billion dollars. C direct equals seven thousand six hundred fifty-five billion dollars

42
00:05:26.000 --> 00:05:34.420
annually. Every second of every day, humanity spends two hundred forty-two thousand six hundred dollars on killing each

43
00:05:34.520 --> 00:05:40.740
other and cleaning up the mess. While you read this sentence, you spent about one point two million dollars.

44
00:05:41.520 --> 00:05:44.940
By the time you feel bad about that, another million is gone.

45
00:05:45.320 --> 00:05:54.070
Military Hardware: The World's Worst Investment. If weapons were a stock, here is the prospectus: Expected annual return:

46
00:05:54.940 --> 00:06:02.240
zero percent. If actually used, return: negative one hundred percent (everything explodes, including the investment).

47
00:06:03.320 --> 00:06:08.740
Maintenance costs: five hundred seventy-nine point eight billion dollars per year.

48
00:06:09.500 --> 00:06:15.460
Useful life: ten to twenty years before obsolescence. Salvage value: zero dollars.

49
00:06:16.240 --> 00:06:22.080
Exit strategy: Death. Investor profile: Nations with more money than sense.

50
00:06:23.220 --> 00:06:30.700
Side effects: May accidentally destroy civilization. Competitive dynamics: Makes neighbors buy the same product.

51
00:06:31.640 --> 00:06:38.910
Success condition: Only "works" if it is never used (if you use nuclear weapons, you have already failed).

52
00:06:39.700 --> 00:06:45.200
No rational investor would touch this. You put trillions into it annually.

53
00:06:46.060 --> 00:06:51.500
The Dead Capital Problem. Normal money grows. You plant an apple tree, you get apples.

54
00:06:52.100 --> 00:06:57.920
You build a factory, you get products. You invest in a hospital, people live longer and pay more taxes.

55
00:06:58.560 --> 00:07:05.000
Military money sits in a warehouse, rusts, becomes obsolete, and has negative net value.

56
00:07:05.720 --> 00:07:10.740
If used, it destroys value, creates rebuilding bills, and kills your customers.

57
00:07:11.380 --> 00:07:17.540
It is the only investment where success means you wasted your money, and failure means everyone is dead.

58
00:07:18.640 --> 00:07:26.640
President Eisenhower (who defeated the Nazis) explained this in nineteen fifty-three: "Every gun that is made, every warship

59
00:07:26.640 --> 00:07:34.620
launched, every rocket fired signifies, in the final sense, a theft from those who hunger and are not fed, those who are

60
00:07:34.780 --> 00:07:44.140
cold and are not clothed." A bomb is not an asset. It is a very expensive liability, like filling your garage with dynamite

61
00:07:44.140 --> 00:07:49.170
and calling it "home security.". This is not pacifism. This is accounting.

62
00:07:50.760 --> 00:07:59.240
The Price of a Ghost: Valuing Human Life. The U.S. Department of Transportation says a statistical life is worth thirteen

63
00:07:59.240 --> 00:08:03.980
point six million dollars. The E.P.A. says nine point six million dollars.

64
00:08:04.560 --> 00:08:09.100
Two government agencies, both American, cannot agree on what you are worth.

65
00:08:09.500 --> 00:08:12.500
A four million dollar disagreement over the price of a person.

66
00:08:13.260 --> 00:08:18.800
We will split the difference and say ten million dollars, which is generous for a species that keeps blowing itself up.

67
00:08:19.740 --> 00:08:28.400
Annual Mortality Cost Calculation. Active combat results in two hundred thirty-four thousand deaths per year at an annual

68
00:08:28.400 --> 00:08:34.400
cost of two point three four trillion dollars, according to Armed Conflict Location and Event Data.

69
00:08:35.500 --> 00:08:42.100
Terror attacks result in eight thousand three hundred deaths per year at an annual cost of eighty-three billion dollars,

70
00:08:42.600 --> 00:08:49.740
according to the Global Terrorism Database. State violence results in two thousand seven hundred deaths per year at an annual

71
00:08:49.740 --> 00:08:54.160
cost of twenty-seven billion dollars, according to the Uppsala Conflict Data Program.

72
00:08:55.360 --> 00:09:00.130
Total Human Cost: two point four five trillion dollars annually.

73
00:09:01.020 --> 00:09:04.460
Two hundred forty-five thousand people die in conflicts each year.

74
00:09:05.020 --> 00:09:10.500
That is six hundred seventy people every day. One every two point two minutes.

75
00:09:11.400 --> 00:09:18.860
Each worth ten million dollars, apparently. Infrastructure Destruction: Building Things, Then Un-Building Them.

76
00:09:19.760 --> 00:09:23.800
When humans fight, they break things. Big things. Expensive things.

77
00:09:24.380 --> 00:09:29.380
Things they spent decades building. Things that took international loans to finance.

78
00:09:29.860 --> 00:09:32.920
Things they will take out new international loans to rebuild.

79
00:09:33.880 --> 00:09:41.920
Reconstruction Cost Analysis (2023 Estimates). Transportation Networks account for four hundred eighty-seven point three

80
